Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 2.1.0
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Fits one cell-type-level Pando design across conditions for
    Human-GEM or Mouse-GEM GPR target genes in paired single-cell RNA and ATAC
    data. Condition-sparse coefficients use the same TF-peak-target edge
    dictionary and equal-condition transforms with nested outer-heldout
    projections. Pando supplies the single canonical pando_condition_grn_fit
    contract with absolute condition effects only; version-suffixed schemas and
    reference-condition contrasts do not enter RegCompass. Non-estimable edge
    contributions are structural zeros in the primary projection path and enter
    target aggregation, metacell means, GPR aggregation, reaction expression and
    penalty construction. Metacells are constructed within condition by broad
    cell type with one fixed gamma across all cells and strata (default 30),
    without top-one-percent depth rejection or depth-dependent gamma adjustment.
    RNA latent-expression priors are estimated separately for each broad cell
    type. A non-finite Pando regulatory modifier falls back exactly to RNA-only
    support and is annotated in the result. The regulatory link uses the single
    canonical value regulatory_alpha = 1. GPR aggregation follows COMPASS:
    complete AND branches use the selected AND rule and OR isozyme branches are
    summed while unavailable branches are ignored. Missing final reaction
    expression is set to zero before penalty conversion and therefore receives
    the maximum expression-linked penalty. Annotation-defined biological
    meta-modules are deduplicated into a merged reaction catalogue. For each
    medium scenario, the package constructs one shared union GEM, performs
    global FASTCORE completion and directional COMPASS-like scoring. Pinned
    human and mouse GEMs are bundled for offline use, with platform-aware
    parallel execution and audited progress and timing output.
